          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mt29xz9dg8h9842k",
          "message": {
            "text": "Escape is a bubble-phase listener, not overlay()'s built-in capture-phase one, on purpose.\n\nThe settings dialog spawns child overlays (theme manager/editor), which are themselves kerfjs/overlay instances that close on their own capture-phase Escape + stopPropagation(). kerf keeps no global overlay stack, so two capture-phase Escape handlers on the same document target don't compose: empirically, with the settings dialog + theme manager stacked, a capture-phase Escape here closed the settings dialog and left the manager open (the exact opposite of what the user expects).\n\nA bubble-phase Escape composes correctly: while a child is open its capture handler stops propagation before the bubble phase, so this never fires; when the settings dialog is topmost, nothing intercepts and it closes normally. This is the same composition the pre-overlay hand-rolled dialog had. We still take overlay()'s focus trap (topmost trap wins, so a child keeps focus — verified) + focus restore + backdrop dismissal.",
            "markdown": "Escape is a bubble-phase listener, not overlay()'s built-in capture-phase one, on purpose.\n\nThe settings dialog spawns child overlays (theme manager/editor), which are themselves kerfjs/overlay instances that close on their own capture-phase Escape + `stopPropagation()`. kerf keeps no global overlay stack, so two capture-phase Escape handlers on the same `document` target don't compose: empirically, with the settings dialog + theme manager stacked, a capture-phase Escape here closed the *settings* dialog and left the manager open (the exact opposite of what the user expects).\n\nA bubble-phase Escape composes correctly: while a child is open its capture handler stops propagation before the bubble phase, so this never fires; when the settings dialog is topmost, nothing intercepts and it closes normally. This is the same composition the pre-overlay hand-rolled dialog had. We still take overlay()'s focus trap (topmost trap wins, so a child keeps focus — verified) + focus restore + backdrop dismissal."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/client/settings/dialog.tsx"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 140,
                  "endLine": 152,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  // Escape is handled by our own BUBBLE-phase listener below, not overlay()'s\n  // built-in (capture-phase) one — the settings dialog spawns child overlays\n  // (theme manager/editor, both kerfjs/overlay), and those close on their own\n  // capture-phase Escape + `stopPropagation()`. A capture-phase Escape here\n  // would race the child's on the same `document` target and could close the\n  // settings dialog out from under an open child (GB-1132). A bubble-phase\n  // listener never fires while a child is open (the child's capture handler\n  // stops propagation first), and fires normally when the dialog is topmost —\n  // the same composition the pre-overlay hand-rolled dialog had. We keep\n  // overlay()'s focus trap (topmost trap wins, so a child keeps focus) + focus\n  // restore + backdrop dismissal.\n  const handle = overlay(() => content.value(), {\n    className: 'modal-overlay', dismiss: ['backdrop'], trap: true,"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
          },
          "workItemUris": [
            "GB-1132"
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "prNoteAnchor/v1": "e9963da6657f5ff2c39d1d1efc0d6bc1"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "warning",
          "guid": "mt29yafaojxnvipv",
          "message": {
            "text": "Inactive tab panels must render EMPTY, or focus escapes the dialog.\n\nkerfjs/overlay's focus trap collects focusables via querySelectorAll and filters only the hidden attribute — it does NOT skip display:none subtrees. Inactive settings panels are display:none via .settings-tab-panel (0), so if their controls were rendered, kerf's computed 'last focusable' would be a hidden control. The browser's native Tab order skips it, so after the last VISIBLE control Tab moves focus OUT of the dialog (kerf's boundary-wrap never triggers because active !== kerf's 'last').\n\nRendering {active ? tab.render(ctx) : null} keeps only visible controls in the trap's cycle. The empty panel div stays for the active-class toggle the e2e tab tests assert on, and a tab switch re-runs this render, so nothing is lost. Verified by the 'focus is trapped' e2e (30 Tabs never leave the overlay).",
            "markdown": "Inactive tab panels must render EMPTY, or focus escapes the dialog.\n\nkerfjs/overlay's focus trap collects focusables via `querySelectorAll` and filters only the `hidden` attribute — it does NOT skip `display:none` subtrees. Inactive settings panels are `display:none` via [.settings-tab-panel](0), so if their controls were rendered, kerf's computed 'last focusable' would be a hidden control. The browser's native Tab order skips it, so after the last VISIBLE control Tab moves focus OUT of the dialog (kerf's boundary-wrap never triggers because active !== kerf's 'last').\n\nRendering `{active ? tab.render(ctx) : null}` keeps only visible controls in the trap's cycle. The empty panel div stays for the active-class toggle the e2e tab tests assert on, and a tab switch re-runs this render, so nothing is lost. Verified by the 'focus is trapped' e2e (30 Tabs never leave the overlay)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/client/settings/dialog.tsx"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 924,
                  "endLine": 933,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "          // Only the active panel renders its interactive content. Inactive\n          // panels are `display:none` (so their controls aren't visible), but\n          // kerfjs/overlay's focus trap detects focusables by DOM query and does\n          // NOT skip `display:none` subtrees — leaving them rendered would put\n          // hidden controls in the trap's tab cycle and let focus escape the\n          // dialog (GB-1132). The empty panel div stays for the active-class\n          // toggle; a tab switch re-runs this render, so nothing is lost.\n          <div className={`settings-tab-panel${tab.id === activeTabId ? ' active' : ''}`} data-panel={tab.id}>\n            {tab.id === activeTabId ? tab.render(ctx) : null}\n          </div>"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
