          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mt29yh2qny5yrpby",
          "message": {
            "text": "The GB-1130 height pin is a signal read in the template, not an imperative style.\n\nUnder overlay() the .modal div is part of the mounted template (the wrapper is the mount root), so a modalEl.style.minHeight = ... set imperatively would be clobbered on the next child morph. Making min-height a signal the template reads means kerf's morph preserves it. The measurement loop runs while minHeight is null so each tab renders at natural height; the max is then written to the signal, re-rendering with the pin applied — same 'tallest tab wins, shorter tabs get bottom slack' behavior as before, just morph-safe.",
            "markdown": "The GB-1130 height pin is a signal read in the template, not an imperative style.\n\nUnder overlay() the `.modal` div is part of the mounted template (the wrapper is the mount root), so a `modalEl.style.minHeight = ...` set imperatively would be clobbered on the next child morph. Making min-height a signal the template reads means kerf's morph preserves it. The measurement loop runs while `minHeight` is null so each tab renders at natural height; the max is then written to the signal, re-rendering with the pin applied — same 'tallest tab wins, shorter tabs get bottom slack' behavior as before, just morph-safe."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/client/settings/dialog.tsx"
                },
